IFCONFIG(8)                    P32W Unix                     IFCONFIG(8)

NAME
       ifconfig - the network interface

SYNOPSIS
       ifconfig
       ifconfig dhcp
       ifconfig addr [netmask m] [gateway g] [dns d]

DESCRIPTION
       With no arguments, ifconfig shows the network coprocessor's
       interface, net0: whether its link is up, whether its address
       came by DHCP, its MAC address, and the address, netmask,
       gateway and DNS server.

       As root, ifconfig dhcp gets them by DHCP (the coprocessor does
       that at start-up), and ifconfig addr sets a fixed address:
       what is not given stays as it was (netmask 255.255.255.0 if
       there was none). It then shows the result.

EXAMPLES
       ifconfig 192.168.1.32 gateway 192.168.1.1 dns 192.168.1.1
              a fixed address on a home network

SEE ALSO
       ping(8), netctl(2), socket(2)

BUGS
       One interface. The setting is lost when the coprocessor
       restarts. In the emulators (p32emu -N) the addresses are QEMU's:
       P32W is 10.0.2.15 and the Mac is 10.0.2.2, and setting them
       changes only what is reported.
